ally exciting and and it's  something that I've really enjoyed being  a part of because I feel like when for  me you know working in film was always  about the theatrical experience I mean  it's you're getting a tell a story a  modern storytelling is in a theater with  a whole bunch of people and this is this  is a reason to get the sitter in and you  know pay the valet and and you know and  go out there and see it because you're  really getting an incredible experience  that premium experience is what people  want I think and I love that IMAX is so  passionate about the image quality and  the presentation and the brightness of  their projectors and and everything else  and so you know that if you're buying an  IMAX ticket that you're gonna get a good  quality resolve you're not going to be  sitting there going like oh man  and I couldn't see what was going on in  the corner over there because the  projector was blurry or whatever that  doesn't happen so I'm a big fan  do you remember the first IMAX movie you  ever saw oh my gosh I I definitely saw  stuff at the Science Center back in the  day the big one for Oh screen movie it  was I remember being blown away I can't  remember what it was was one of the  museum pieces for sure but yeah I don't  recall which one it was to be honest but  but obviously it had an impact well I  just was blown away but I'd never been  in a theater like that I mean at the  time to the stadium seating and all that  stuff that was all new I mean nobody had  done that and to be sitting in a with a  screen that was like below the floor and  above the ceiling and you know it's like  incredible so to me you know that's a  that's a very different way to see  cinema you know if you could pick any  film ever to remaster into IMAX what  would it be hmm Wow Wow  I'm kind of I'm kind of guessing you've  done some of these right some of the  ones that are thinking I don't know when  you said that 2001 popped into my head  right away which seems like 